    "result_text": "Green. The full suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the disposable-domain blocklist rule for `POST /api/owners` following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (no Spring MVC controllers).\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/RequireEmailDomain.java` \u2014 validation step reading the shared `OwnerFieldsDto` via `@Val`; rejects when the email's domain (case-insensitive) is in the blocklist `{mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}`. Absent/blank email is left untouched (email is optional), mirroring `NormalizeOwnerEmail`/`RequirePostcode`.\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) carrying the offending value.\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with body `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, matching the existing `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring:** Inserted a `requireEmailDomain` step into `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` right after `normalizeEmail`, so the domain check runs against the already-trimmed/lower-cased/syntactically-validated value, before address normalization and the persistence steps.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`) returns 400, and the whole suite is green.",
